# ==== .spiceinit (exact) ====
| * ngspice init settings for the sky130 PDK model libraries.
| *
| * The corner runner copies this file into its scratch run directory as
| * `.spiceinit` before invoking ngspice, so runs do not depend on whatever
| * happens to be in ~/.spiceinit. To drive ngspice by hand with the same
| * settings, copy this file to `.spiceinit` in your working directory.
| *
| * Derived from the PDK's own libs.tech/ngspice/spinit; kept in-repo so the
| * settings a record was produced under are versioned with the harness.
| 
| set ngbehavior=hsa     ; HSPICE-ish compatibility, required to read PDK libs
| set skywaterpdk        ; skip some checks for faster lib loading
| set ng_nomodcheck      ; do not check model parameters
| option noinit          ; do not dump operating point data into the log
| option klu             ; KLU direct linear solver

# ==== deck (exact input given to ngspice) ====
| * trim-lsb-chained deck (process=ss, supply=3.3) -- generated by sim/trim-lsb-chained/run_trim_lsb_chained.py, do not edit
| .option wnflag=1 reltol=1e-6 vntol=1e-9 abstol=1e-15
| .param vsup=3.3
| .lib "/Users/rwalters/.volare/sky130A/libs.tech/combined/sky130.lib.spice" ss
| ** sch_path: sim/output-voltage-tc/testbench/tb_vref_tc.sch
| **.subckt tb_vref_tc
| V1 VDD 0 'vsup'
| .save i(v1)
| XBG VREF GDRV VDD 0 bandgap_core
| **** begin user architecture code
| 
| 
| * DC-solver seed, not a forced solution: see the header note. Without it the
| * solver can settle on the core's degenerate zero-current state, which is
| * what issue #10's startup circuit exists to prevent in silicon.
| .nodeset v(vref)=1.2 v(gdrv)=2.2
| 
| 
| **** end user architecture code
| **.ends
| 
| * expanding   symbol:  design/bandgap_core.sym # of pins=4
| ** sym_path: design/bandgap_core.sym
| ** sch_path: design/bandgap_core.sch
| .subckt bandgap_core VOUT GDRV VDD VSS
| *.opin VOUT
| *.iopin GDRV
| *.iopin VDD
| *.iopin VSS
| **** begin user architecture code
| 
| 
| * ---- Kuijk core parameters (issue #8) ----
| * PNP emitter-area ratio N is built ONLY from paralleled unit devices:
| *   N = (n_pnp_ptat * 11.56 um2) / (n_pnp_ctat * 0.4624 um2)
| * Keep both counts equal to hold the pair's measured dVBE while lowering the
| * per-unit current and sigma(dVBE); raise n_pnp_ptat alone for more PTAT.
| .param n_pnp_ctat=8
| .param n_pnp_ptat=8
| * res_high_po unit segment: W = r_w um, L = r_lseg um (R ~ 380 + 325*L ohm)
| .param r_w=1
| .param r_lseg=5
| * segment counts. K = R2/R1 is set by the integer ratio n_r2/n_r1.
| .param n_r1=7
| .param n_r2=54
| * PMOS mirror multiplicities (unit device W=8u L=2u)
| .param m_out=2
| .param m_ampbias=2
| * ---- Trim network (issue #13), DOWNWARD ONLY -- see DR-002 ----
| * Ladder-tap length added to R2A/R2B equally (metal option, no switches).
| * n_r2_trim: valid range 0..-16 only. r_lseg_trim: 1 um/code (~1.7 mV/code).
| * Positive codes are REJECTED: this is the same R2/R1 ratio issue #46 found
| * causes ff/2.97V, fs/2.97V hot-corner (>~123C) operating-point collapse at
| * even a +5 um increase (n_r2=55). sim/trim-range-monotonicity/ reconfirms
| * it for trim and finds codes +1/+2 ALSO collapse (VOUT -> ~2.8V) while +3/
| * +4 happen not to -- non-monotonic-in-code, i.e. no positive code is a
| * certified-safe point, not a safe zone at +3/+4. Only downward (R2
| * decrease) moves away from that edge; confirmed monotonic, collapse-free
| * to -16 across corners. See DR-002 and the sim record for the full case.
| .param n_r2_trim=0
| .param r_lseg_trim=1
| 
| 
